      "title": "Translation candidate source — one interface, many engines",
      "description": "The one interface every candidate-translation engine meets: for a layer's catalogues, append candidate translations per string to the `translation-candidates/v1` sidecar, each carrying its source, and seed an empty `msgstr` with the first candidate marked fuzzy. An agent model and the open machine-translation engines (OPUS-MT, LibreTranslate / Argos) are interchangeable behind it. Use when adding an engine, choosing one, or producing candidates for review.",
